B5.1.5.1.1 Determine the percentage of a given quantity (limit to 2-digit whole number) and vice versa

E.g. 1  Review multiplying a fraction by a whole number.  e.g. 2/5 × 10 means shade 2 × (1/5 𝑜𝑓 10) ;

 i.e. 2×(2) = 4;

E.g. 2 To multiply a percent fraction by a whole number, change the percentage to common fraction and multiply and simplify e.g.40% × 10 means (40/100 𝑜𝑓 10) = 4;

E.g. 3 Ask learners to find given percentage of given quantities; e.g. What is 20% of 45?

What is 20% of 45?
20% of 45 = 20% × 45
= 20/100 × 45/1
= 9
